|----|--------------|--------------|------------|
| 1  | 63           | 69           | 6          |
| 2  | 65           | 65           | 0          |
| 3  | 56           | 62           | 6          |
| 4  | 100          | 91           | -9         |
| 5  | 88           | 78           | -10        |
| 6  | 83           | 87           | 4          |
| 7  | 77           | 79           | 2          |
| 8  | 92           | 88           | -4         |
| 9  | 90           | 85           | -5         |
| 10 | 84           | 92           | 8          |
| 11 | 68           | 69           | 1          |
| 12 | 74           | 81           | 7          |
| 13 | 87           | 84           | -3         |
| 14 | 64           | 75           | 11         |
| 15 | 71           | 84           | 13         |
| 16 | 88           | 82           | -6         |
| **SUM** | 1250 | 1271 | 21 |
| **MEAN** |78.13 | 79.44 | 1.31 |
| **Standard deviation** | 12.66 | 9.15 | 7.00 |


1. What hypothesis method should be applied to find out whether the two exams are equally difficult or not?  
<br><br>

2. What are the degrees of freedom?  
<br><br>

3. Please test the hypotheses and draw a conclusion (alpha = 0.01).
